    <item>
      <title>Netflix Sales Growth to Decline for Fourth Quarter in a Row</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/news/videos/2026-10-20/netflix-forecasts-adds-to-growth-concerns-video</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">7d6c01f76528ede40ebe8429</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:58:49 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>Netflix reported earnings for the third quarter that exceeded Wall Street expectations, but forecast a fourth consecutive quarter of slowing sales growth, a projection that may amplify concerns about the performance of the world’s leading online TV network. Netflix delivered sales of $12.9 billion in the third quarter, in line with Wall Street’s expectations, and forecast sales of $13.4 billion in the year’s final three months, falling short of what analysts have predicted. The pace of growth has fallen from 17.6% in the final quarter of last year to a projection of 11.5% for this year’s fourth quarter. The company blamed its sales shortfall on the advertising business, which is on pace to deliver $300 million less than the company expected. Bloomberg Tech Host Ed Ludlow joins Bloomberg Businessweek Daily to discuss. He speaks with Alexis Christoforous and Norah Mulinda. (Source: Bloomberg)</description>
      <wire:publisher>Bloomberg</wire:publisher>
